\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Within Segal categories (this document), colimits, initial objects, left Kan extensions, left adjoints are obtained by the \code{to_dual} attribute (→ \ref{dec-tl-0003}), which acts by \code{op} on shapes and on the ambient Segal category. No dual notion at this layer is defined by hand. Scope: \code{to_dual} is total on Segal categories and on the \em{horizontal} op of VDC∞s (reversal of inputs); the vertical op is not available for augmented VDC∞s (nullary-target cells have no nullary-source dual) and transpose is not available for virtual ones, so in → \ref{ft-0000} some dual statements will be proved by hand and the attribute records that they are duals rather than generating them. \code{Cᵒᵖᵒᵖ ≃ C} is an equivalence, never an identity, past the seal; \code{to_dual}'s transport lemmas along it are part of the attribute's output.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-up-0005}: \code{to_dual} of \code{Limit} is a colimit in the classical sense for discrete \code{C}.}
}
